==Portuguese==
{{wikipedia|lang=pt}}
[[Image:Surface anatomy of the heart.png|thumb|200px|coração]]

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|coraçon||heart}}, from a derivative of {{inh|pt|la|cor||heart}} with the suffix {{m|pt|-ção|-ação}}, either through a {{inh|pt|VL.|-}} root {{m|la||*corātiō}}, {{m|la||*corātiōne}} or {{m|la||*coraceōne}}. Ultimately from {{inh|pt|itc-pro|*kord}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*ḱḗr}} ~ {{m|ine-pro||*ḱr̥d-}}.

Cognate with Aragonese {{m|an|corazón}}, Asturian {{m|ast|corazón}}, Galician {{m|gl|corazón}}, Ladino {{m|lad|korasón}}, Leonese {{m|roa-leo|corazón}}, Mirandese {{m|mwl|coraçon}}, Mozarabic {{m|mxi|corachón}} and Spanish {{m|es|corazón}} (Old Spanish {{m|osp|coraçon}}).

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|Brazil}} {{IPA|/ko.ɾa.ˈsɐ̃w̃/|lang=pt}}
* {{a|Portugal}} {{IPA|/ku.ɾɐ.ˈsɐ̃w̃/|lang=pt}}
*: {{audio|pt-pt-coração.ogg|Audio (PT)|lang=pt}}
*: {{homophones|lang=pt|curação|Curação}}
* {{hyphenation|co|ra|ção|lang=pt}}

